  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Sunday)\nIssued at 206 PM MDT Mon Jul 27 2026\n\nConvective outflows and remnant MCVs from the storms Tuesday will \nprovide additional lift for storms Wednesday. There is no notable \nchange in the placement of the H5 high center over eastern NM and \nlittle change to mid level temps or steering flow. The NBM90th \npercentile QPF envelope trends a little lower Wednesday but many\nfootprints are still >0.75\" in several areas around the higher \nterrain. These amounts will likely trend higher as hi-res CAMs \nget into the mix. More Heat Advisories are also likely for parts \nof the area. \n\nBy Thursday, the H5 high is shown drifting west into central NM \nwhile strengthening to near 598dm. This will most likely result in a \nslight downtick in storm coverage with a return to greater coverage \nof Heat Advisories. A repeat in convection over eastern CO Thursday \nmay force another boundary southwest into eastern NM Thursday night. \nThis would spark another uptick in storm coverage Friday and perhaps \nSaturday as the H5 high center drifts west into northeast AZ.",
